A||||8||Bens88GT||Where can I buy a 1" rear swaybar for my 88GT?||||5||
Z||000000||Bens88GT||07-23-2000||12:51 PM||||Someone said a while ago that they put a 1" rear bar on their 88GT, but all I can find anywhere is the stock 7/8" bar. Anyone know? Thanks!<P>-Ben||||reg||5
Z||000001||88formula||07-23-2000||02:08 PM||||Performance Suspension Technology. Do a search on the net.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bens88GT||07-23-2000||03:05 PM||||Hey, thanks a lot! That's just what I was looking for! For anyone else that's looking for the same thing, here's the URL:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.p-s-t.com/sway.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.p-s-t.com/sway.html</A> <P>-Ben||||reg||10
Z||000003||Megafiero||07-23-2000||10:25 PM||||I think you can get it from <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fierostore.com/</A> <BR>check their website, if you don't see it,  try giving them a call.<P>Megafiero||||reg||1
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||07-23-2000||11:57 PM||||Ryane sells the Addco 1" rear bar too. I have it on the rear of my 88 and I like it. If you do go with the 1" bar you will need to drill a new hole to mount the saddles because their new saddle holes are farther apart than the factory ones.||||reg||1
Z||000005||AL||07-24-2000||09:41 PM|||| <A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=522257&a=3823750&p=24977743" TARGET=_blank>http://albums.photopoint.com/j/ViewPhoto?u=522257&a=3823750&p=24977743</A>  <BR>hey ben this is how it will look. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||07-24-2000||11:38 PM||||Won't look like that... not on an 88. The 88 has a factory rear bar and it sits on top of the cradle and has brackets that connect it to the struts. It looks cleaner tucked up in there but it's a pain to install it.<P><p>[This message has been edited by SCCA FIERO (edited 07-24-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Bens88GT||07-24-2000||11:59 PM||||Hey guys, did the 1" bar make your Fiero's handling close to neutral, or did it actually give it some oversteer? I want to know if this bar is overkill, or if some poly endlinks would do it.<P>Thanks!<BR>-Ben||||reg||5
Z||000008||SCCA FIERO||07-25-2000||12:12 AM||||On the track it feel better than none at all. It's easy to "put the rearend where you want it". I can only compare it to not having a rear swaybar at all. My 88 Coupe didn't have one (of course) and I have only had this 1" bar on it. The front bar is also 1" on my Coupe and I am not sure how big the front bar is on the Formula/GT. I plan to get a 1.25" front bar to see what happens.<P>BTW, my Coupe does have a V6 so the weight is about the same as yours. If you hate the "push" you get when trying to turn on the gas, then get the 1" bar. The 1" bar on mine make it funner... can you say "power-on oversteer???"<P>------------------<BR>-Chris <BR>88 Fiero Coupe||||reg||1
